# AGENTS.md — __AOH_TITLE__

A user-owned Temporal **activity** worker for WFE (scaffolded from the
`aoh-wfe-worker` skill). It runs the activities a WFE workflow schedules; it is
not the WFE engine or manager.

## Load-bearing rules

- **Activities only.** The worker runs with `DisableWorkflowWorker` — the mirror
  of the engine's `LocalActivityWorkerOnly`. Do not register workflows here;
  workflows live in the WFE workflow-engine.
- **Two contracts with the engine:** (1) `temporal.task_queue` must match the
  engine's (default `wfe`); (2) an activity is addressed by its Go **method
  name**, which is the string a DSL `Activity.Type` (and the `service_activity` /
  `service_event` registry) uses. Renaming a method is a contract change — mirror
  it in `sql/seed_catalog.sql`.
- **Keep activities cancellable.** Long-running activities must heartbeat
  (`activity.RecordHeartbeat`) and return on `ctx.Done()`, so a workflow can
  cancel them.
- **One starter activity + one starter event out of the box.** `HelloWorld` (an
  activity) and `Timer` (a long-running, cancellable timer event) in
  `internal/activities/activities.go` are illustrative — events are worker methods
  too, just catalogued in `service_event`. Replace them with yours, keep them
  registered in `cmd/worker/main.go`, and seed them.

## Conventions

Standard AOH Go service conventions apply (Viper config, `aoh-golib` logger +
health + Temporal client, the shipped `.golangci.yml`). The `aoh-conventions`
skill's `references/go.md` is the source of truth.
